cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Pocketscribe: confidence-aware binding-pocket triage and molecular dynamics
  setup for predicted protein structures
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it together with the tools it
  integrates. Pocketscribe introduces no new pocket-detection algorithm,
  druggability model or force field; fpocket, GROMACS, CHARMM36m and the
  structure-prediction models do that work, and each is listed under
  "references" below and in the README's "Built on" section.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: John
    family-names: Adedeji
    name-particle: Adeyemo
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1257-4551'
    affiliation: 'Osun State University, Osogbo, Osun State, Nigeria'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/jonahnki/pocketscribe'
url: 'https://github.com/jonahnki/pocketscribe'
abstract: >-
  Pocketscribe takes a protein structure predicted by AlphaFold2, OpenFold,
  ColabFold, ESMFold or Boltz and produces a single self-contained report
  covering structure quality control, binding-pocket detection, druggability
  scoring caveated by the prediction's own per-residue confidence, optional
  cross-model pocket consensus, and ready-to-run GROMACS input files. Its
  distinguishing feature is treating per-residue prediction confidence as a
  first-class signal that caveats every downstream pocket claim, rather than
  analysing a predicted structure as if it were experimental. Its cross-model
  consensus module scores pocket agreement in an architecture-family-aware way,
  reporting agreement between independent method families separately from, and
  as stronger evidence than, agreement within one family. Research use only.
keywords:
  - structural biology
  - drug discovery
  - binding site prediction
  - pocket detection
  - molecular dynamics
  - AlphaFold
  - ESMFold
  - ColabFold
  - protein structure prediction
  - research software
license: MIT
